  "$schema": "folio-block-summaries/v1",
  "entry": "10665-338849",
  "summaries": [
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-000",
      "source": "sections/sec-000-antecedentes.md",
      "source_hash": "3760cd7957932f82845a18db21c64b8a2d3c514c9100086775886e5e72da4a3e",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that this interim guidance on the Pfizer–BioNTech COVID-19 vaccine is based on advice from WHO's Strategic Advisory Group of Experts on Immunization (SAGE) at its 5 January 2021 meeting, with declarations of interest reviewed.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-001",
      "source": "sections/sec-001-métodos.md",
      "source_hash": "86f240879b0dfda7fed48e77e81cdf4d817d2d903b136ccb693aee416a79014e",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that SAGE follows an evidence-based process for its recommendations and uses a specific framework for assessing clinical trial evidence on COVID-19 vaccines.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-002",
      "source": "sections/sec-002-objetivo-y-estrategia-generales-para-la-utilizac.md",
      "source_hash": "d8ec60ffac5687ed9a3ef50f4f2dd0ba4583663ab2024c3108446687ddd7f935",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Sets out the overall aim and strategy for using the BNT162b2 mRNA vaccine, noting it was the first COVID-19 vaccine given WHO emergency use listing on 31 December 2020 and showed about 95% efficacy. It advises countries to use the WHO prioritisation roadmap and values framework while supply is limited, starting with high-risk health workers and older people.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-003",
      "source": "sections/sec-003-uso-previsto.md",
      "source_hash": "d7b0a078fed5125ce66e01ae709b621ac478b364e015cfaba12cd535ce49f692",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "States that the vaccine is intended for people aged 16 years and over.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-004",
      "source": "sections/sec-004-aplicación.md",
      "source_hash": "9f36887fe974870a49be3483b02be19a0637d8a2360caa71100440907408336e",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Recommends giving the vaccine as two 30 µg intramuscular doses in the deltoid, 21 to 28 days apart, with guidance on doses given early or late and a limit of two doses in total.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-005",
      "source": "sections/sec-005-aspectos-que-deben-tenerse-en-cuenta-para-aplaza.md",
      "source_hash": "5732ffe66b0f1ac5875d4a10516a43f26a0bf3b41b9af585562a40fa33e463e8",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Discusses whether countries facing scarce supply and high disease burden could delay the second dose to reach more people with a first dose, noting efficacy starts about 12 days after dose one. Because long-term single-dose data are lacking, WHO currently advises that the interval between doses not exceed 42 days.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-006",
      "source": "sections/sec-006-dosis-de-refuerzo.md",
      "source_hash": "7fc9387e77c6990cd2d4cc3cfdee6ef442db0a12060f127e8366a72f3d8b2891",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that there is no evidence yet on whether booster doses will be needed after the two-dose series.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-007",
      "source": "sections/sec-007-intercambiabilidad-con-las-demás-vacunas.md",
      "source_hash": "377f8b19597eac756efd9abee5ce2dd9edb882ca6b4395c5acd1e15065936a05",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "States that no data exist on interchanging this vaccine with other COVID-19 vaccines, so the same product should be used for both doses and no extra doses are advised if products are mixed by mistake.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-008",
      "source": "sections/sec-008-administración-simultánea-con-otras-vacunas.md",
      "source_hash": "3ff1f2a47e0a1330f95bb163bb10db3ebbb2fd502b3f226c381d3e0d75bf14a5",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Advises leaving at least 14 days between this vaccine and any other vaccine until data on co-administration are available.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-009",
      "source": "sections/sec-009-contraindicaciones.md",
      "source_hash": "a61b1842155c3f206eed9f936ed4f964b0986ba92c08207e7728cf1b0cad5432",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "States that a history of severe allergic reaction to any vaccine component, particularly polyethylene glycol, is a contraindication.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-010",
      "source": "sections/sec-010-precauciones.md",
      "source_hash": "6f35625be46181f1c011d7c1d2ba3f1bd54f09be1195df21bd95d4d8b7e1c5bb",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Sets out precautions after reports of anaphylaxis, advising risk assessment and 30 minutes of observation for people with prior immediate allergic reactions to other vaccines or injectable drugs. It recommends vaccinating only where anaphylaxis can be treated, observing all recipients for at least 15 minutes, and postponing vaccination during acute febrile illness, while food, latex, egg and gelatin allergies need no special precautions.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-013",
      "source": "sections/sec-013-personas-mayores.md",
      "source_hash": "e9da9547da02fa37cc7ab7e03e5462cf352f4fe183235994ac408ce6516d6d4f",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Recommends vaccinating older people, noting phase 3 data show similar efficacy and safety across age groups from 16 years.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-014",
      "source": "sections/sec-014-personas-que-presenten-enfermedades-concomitante.md",
      "source_hash": "5741e12991e292ce2532ec06442462544ba17af31208925f93a403c97d1bcdbb",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Recommends vaccinating people with comorbidities that raise the risk of severe COVID-19, noting trials showed similar safety and efficacy in people with conditions such as hypertension, diabetes, asthma and well-controlled HIV or hepatitis. The conditions studied in the phase 2 and 3 trials are listed.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-015",
      "source": "sections/sec-015-grupos-demográficos-para-los-que-no-se-dispone-d.md",
      "source_hash": "70a42745fe128c72d06b3d96887ac2de6cb567ccb24111b3327b25aba0791b4f",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A heading fragment for the section on groups with limited trial data, containing only two words.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-016",
      "source": "sections/sec-016-pacientes-mayores-de-85-años-de-edad.md",
      "source_hash": "216d4164f4e828c552802328cfb5f223575b161807214a2e8710ede3c261cc7d",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Recommends vaccinating older people with no upper age limit, although people over 85 and very frail older people were not included in trials.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-017",
      "source": "sections/sec-017-niños-y-adolescentes-menores-de-16-años-de-edad.md",
      "source_hash": "8d4136724bc3eb77a81c357f3159b2a24b022b8b0b44338ca43c733247e2a867",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Advises against vaccinating children and adolescents under 16 until data on efficacy and safety become available.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-018",
      "source": "sections/sec-018-embarazadas.md",
      "source_hash": "96f965b3fc31a5bd0709fab3a6ec186c071eefd95158dd250a4d0028d84eebdc",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that pregnant women face higher risk of severe COVID-19 but data on the vaccine in pregnancy are insufficient, though animal studies showed no harm. WHO advises against use in pregnancy unless benefits outweigh risks, such as for high-exposure health workers or women with comorbidities, and does not recommend pregnancy testing before vaccination.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-019",
      "source": "sections/sec-019-mujeres-lactantes.md",
      "source_hash": "b6eb3bab9bf88bfda92c32eab9617fdd5a8e18b56b58376413d0981acf6d8fc5",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "States that the vaccine should be offered to breastfeeding women in priority groups on the same basis as others, since the mRNA is unlikely to pose a risk to breastfed infants. WHO does not advise stopping breastfeeding after vaccination.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-020",
      "source": "sections/sec-020-personas-infectadas-por-el-vih.md",
      "source_hash": "38937bb3189d274f4d81d01408e19a51c1b83fd680cec3182ba2ada0e2be76d3",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Allows vaccination of people with well-controlled HIV in priority groups, noting no difference in safety signals in trials but insufficient data for those not on treatment. It advises providing information for individual risk–benefit decisions and says HIV testing before vaccination is not needed.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-021",
      "source": "sections/sec-021-personas-inmunodeprimidas.md",
      "source_hash": "4acd29a2a2cf5ed0ab17a2552d5de8d9057a06e3e9ef16c7100b700509fa17c9",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Allows vaccination of immunocompromised people in priority groups because the vaccine contains no live virus, while noting that data are lacking and responses may be weaker, and advises informed individual decisions.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-022",
      "source": "sections/sec-022-personas-que-presentan-enfermedades-autoinmunita.md",
      "source_hash": "1c5a824aeda6958b9883f4566446794136a7c140cb350d0ec1300a95a0cd9a98",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes the lack of data on people with autoimmune conditions and allows them to be vaccinated if they have no contraindication.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-023",
      "source": "sections/sec-023-personas-con-antecedentes-de-parálisis-facial.md",
      "source_hash": "4b535ea7ccfaebb80777fad700bb86e7d0cb0467add12b010053193d003d0559",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that facial paralysis was reported in some trial participants without conclusive evidence of a causal link, and allows vaccination of people with a history of facial paralysis.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-024",
      "source": "sections/sec-024-personas-que-anteriormente-presentaron-una-infec.md",
      "source_hash": "ff56a94a57c627ff933b12ada6781d77d4dcb1acd90c311e988e4191f79badb9",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "States that the vaccine can be offered regardless of prior SARS-CoV-2 infection and that testing for previous infection is not recommended before vaccination. Since symptomatic reinfection within six months appears rare, people with confirmed recent infection may choose to delay vaccination until near the end of that period.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-025",
      "source": "sections/sec-025-personas-que-al-momento-de-la-aplicación-de-la-v.md",
      "source_hash": "39fc9a4134da26b6acb9018dd88fe9365c9e772dcc6489722d9114281b6619f3",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Advises postponing vaccination of people with acute symptomatic COVID-19 until they have recovered and meet criteria for ending isolation.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-026",
      "source": "sections/sec-026-personas-a-las-que-anteriormente-se-les-administ.md",
      "source_hash": "3329cb63100a11d90a0155a8dadb2f54c20ec106a0cb075676ee30d6bb5738de",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Advises delaying vaccination for at least 90 days after treatment with monoclonal antibodies or convalescent plasma, as a precaution against interference with the vaccine response.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-027",
      "source": "sections/sec-027-situaciones-especiales.md",
      "source_hash": "a65323cbbebbab7fc90f785cc70bf3c87c483baed93f8cb4884e05fc6dd342a3",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Recommends prioritising vaccination for people in crowded settings where physical distancing is impossible, such as refugee camps, prisons and slums, in line with the WHO prioritisation roadmap. It also calls for attention to groups disproportionately affected by COVID-19 or facing health inequities.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-029",
      "source": "sections/sec-029-pruebas-de-detección-del-sars-cov-2.md",
      "source_hash": "243d025c1f4d0332ff84bcfd6a2b4c585783e3884b1e17023b78b5208c1d3212",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that prior vaccination does not affect nucleic acid or antigen tests for current infection, but that spike-protein antibody tests cannot distinguish vaccination from past infection. It says nucleocapsid antibody tests should be used to look for past infection and that antibody testing to check immunity after vaccination is not recommended.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-030",
      "source": "sections/sec-030-función-de-las-vacunas-en-el-marco-de-las-demás.md",
      "source_hash": "c7df1536dc85851d6d03272bc40c1752b988bd3ff35e3bf8472143669a9cd649",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Advises that, as there is no evidence yet that the vaccine reduces transmission, masks, distancing, hand washing and other non-drug measures should continue for vaccinated and unvaccinated people alike.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-031",
      "source": "sections/sec-031-implicación-comunitaria-comunicación-eficaz-y-le.md",
      "source_hash": "82841e8b82ddb3b6705313226a09eb633fafbd73b046bde6bb6775488d52465d",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Stresses that community engagement and effective risk communication are essential to COVID-19 vaccination programmes, with transparent priority-setting based on shared values. It lists communication strategies, especially for groups unfamiliar with or distrustful of health services.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-032",
      "source": "sections/sec-032-aspectos-organizativos-de-la-vacunación.md",
      "source_hash": "31c0647d7980e11feb96bdd08e7f05b07bdf71b4d5c660e47117cfc9cca0dc9c",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes operational challenges of the vaccine's ultra-cold chain, including shipment sizes, use soon after thawing, the right diluent and protection from light. It also covers planning for vaccinating occupational groups and the need for anaphylaxis treatment and storage capacity in low-resource settings.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-033",
      "source": "sections/sec-033-recomendaciones-sobre-la-manera-de-subsanar-las.md",
      "source_hash": "f589ff5cd49f178db84e8879aa7bdb8a44018ddf8e7ebddb21f0fd259ccb0063",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Lists research and surveillance needed to fill knowledge gaps, including active long-term safety monitoring and reporting by Pfizer, BioNTech and vaccine providers of errors, serious adverse events, anaphylaxis, facial paralysis and other events. It calls for studies on effectiveness in specific groups, duration of protection, effect on transmission, co-administration and pregnancy. It also proposes head-to-head comparisons with other vaccines on the size and duration of immunity.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-034",
      "source": "sections/sec-034-referencias.md",
      "source_hash": "dda7a7a865ffe04311bd1e0c3da2b45d7868a55dde6b18497ef183b5ec9123ed",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The reference list, citing the SAGE meeting, SAGE guidance on developing recommendations, the COVID-19 vaccine evidence framework and WHO's prioritisation roadmap and values framework.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-035",
      "source": "sections/sec-035-fuente-de-financiamiento.md",
      "source_hash": "34165e55c65ec94de008148cbf508195b6c5c8f346625e43d165d3d70b209311",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "States that SAGE and working group members are not paid by WHO for their work and that the SAGE secretariat is funded by core contributions to WHO.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-338849/blocks/prose-sec-036",
      "source": "sections/sec-036-nota-de-agradecimiento.md",
      "source_hash": "65df83b3f9b0a6a0613be0c72a04dca46b0a99dc5213b7a8d29297466f876ca1",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Acknowledges the SAGE members and WHO staff consulted, states the guidance stays valid for two years unless updated, and gives the copyright, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 IGO licence and reference number.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
